      en: "Pilgrim's Rest is a historic gold mining town in Mpumalanga, South Africa. Founded in 1873 after the discovery of gold, it quickly became a hub of the gold rush. The town features well-preserved Victorian buildings, including the Royal Hotel and the Church of the Holy Trinity. Declared a national monument in 1986, it now operates as a living open-air museum. The annual Pilgrim's Rest Festival celebrates the gold rush era. Surrounding areas offer hiking in the scenic Drakensberg Mountains.",
