      en: "Church Square in Pretoria, South Africa, is one of the city's oldest squares and of historical significance. At its center stands an equestrian statue of Paul Kruger, former president of the South African Republic. The square is lined with notable buildings including the Old Town Hall (1899), the Palace of Justice (1897), and the Dutch Buildings. Church Square was a site of political rallies and the Boer War. Today it is a popular meeting place and a testament to Victorian architecture. The square is named after the original church that stood there. It is a national heritage site and attracts both tourists and locals.",
